---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-sendlane';
const title = 'Postscript vs Sendlane for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare Sendlane consolidation with a retained Postscript text program: Shopify import, cart suppression, cutover ownership and quote-based costs.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Sendlane replace Postscript for SMS?",
    "answer": "It is a candidate when its demonstrated text workflows meet your requirements. Compare consent migration, reply handling, queued-message suppression and sending eligibility before retiring the existing program; there is no universal volume cutoff."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Postscript offer email now?",
    "answer": "Postscript has announced Email and links to a waitlist. Confirm access and migration scope for your account before treating it as an available replacement for Sendlane email."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should Sendlane and Postscript both send lifecycle SMS?",
    "answer": "Assign each journey one text owner. Splitting lifecycle and promotional text requires explicit consent-state transfer, purchase suppression and a way to stop both senders; otherwise keep the text program with one owner."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Postscript vs Sendlane for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Move email and text together, or stage the migration?</p></header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Choose the scope of the migration first</h2>
        <p>A merchant moving email to Sendlane has two decisions: whether to rebuild email there and whether to move an existing Postscript text program too. Consolidating both channels can reduce coordination work, but changing two senders together increases the cutover surface. Keeping Postscript temporarily can separate the projects, provided the team can operate the shared customer state. Neither architecture establishes a conversion or compliance winner.</p>
        <h2>What the suppliers currently describe</h2>
        <p>Sendlane’s <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/sendlane-app">Shopify listing</a> describes email, SMS and forms together and shows a two-way SMS reply feature. Do not dismiss its SMS as one-way. Postscript has announced <a href="https://postscript.io/launch">Email and links to a waitlist</a>; the old SMS-only description is outdated. Verify access, supported workflows and contract scope for your account before comparing a complete replacement against a text-only project.</p>
        <h2>Inspect the Shopify import before enabling journeys</h2>
        <p>Sendlane’s <a href="https://help.sendlane.com/articles/4961381973-how-to-integrate-shopify-and-sendlane">installation guide</a> describes importing contacts with Shopify activity in the past year, including contacts imported into Shopify during that period. It also advises upgrading a trial before connecting the shop. Budget the evaluation around that dependency rather than promising a free live-store test. An imported customer record is not evidence of marketing permission: reconcile email and SMS subscription records, capture source and suppression history separately.</p>
        <h2>Make cart exit a deliberate configuration decision</h2>
        <p>The same guide identifies an optional setting to remove customers from the abandoned-cart list after purchase. Record whether it is enabled and inspect the actual journey exit as well. Proposed check: let a permitted test customer enter a cart journey, purchase before the next step, then inspect both email and text queues. Repeat with a purchase while the customer is also eligible for a promotional audience. A list removal setting alone does not demonstrate that every queued message in another tool has been canceled.</p>
        <h2>Keep one owner for each text journey</h2>
        <p>If Sendlane takes email while Postscript keeps SMS, write down the owner of welcome text, cart recovery, product launches and replenishment reminders. Avoid casually letting Sendlane send lifecycle SMS while Postscript sends promotions: a customer can qualify for both. Before using that split, document identity matching, opt-out propagation, purchase exclusions and who can pause all text sends. If those transfers cannot be demonstrated, choose one text sender while retaining the email migration as a separate project.</p>
        <h2>Rehearse a limited release without inventing a speed winner</h2>
        <p>Use a draft product-release campaign to examine eligible audience counts, timezone treatment, purchase exclusions, message encoding and pause controls in each proposed setup. Ask the supplier to explain capacity limits for the intended peak and how a partial send is reported. For replies, route a product question and a subscription-change request to the responsible support team; the latter must reach the subscription system rather than being treated as a marketing conversion. These are proposed checks, not observed throughput, deliverability or recovery results.</p>
        <h2>Compare quotes using the same retained work</h2>
        <p>Request written quotes for Sendlane email plus SMS, and for Sendlane email with the intended Postscript program retained. Include expected email sends, text destinations and usage, allowances, minimum commitments, support, onboarding and duplicate capture tools. Model ordinary and promotional periods separately using your own calendar. Do not assume a contact-based bill, free bundled messages or savings against a third provider. Compare total costs with the margin from incremental orders only when you have a credible measurement design; dashboard-attributed revenue can overlap between channels.</p>
        <h2>Cut over with a reversible sender map</h2>
        <p>Archive existing flow logic, templates, consent evidence and suppression exports before rebuilding. Name the last active send from the old journey and the first eligible event for the replacement, including contacts already waiting in delays. Validate the draft configuration with permitted contacts, pause superseded automations and reconcile the first live eligible audiences before expanding. Rollback means restoring the intended owner and its current suppression state, not switching both systems on. Set evaluation timing around renewal and actual workflow risks rather than an arbitrary minimum trial length.</p>
        <h2>Decision and evidence limits</h2>
        <p>Evaluate consolidation when Sendlane demonstrates the required email and text journeys with less coordination work at an acceptable quoted cost. Retain Postscript text when a specific unmet requirement or safer staged migration justifies the extra operation. Evaluate Postscript Email separately if access is confirmed. Supplier descriptions checked November 25, 2026; no live account tests, merchant outcomes, legal ranking or financial winner are claimed. Sender eligibility, contract terms and integration behavior remain account-specific verification work.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sendlane-vs-klaviyo">Sendlane vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/rejoiner-vs-sendlane">Rejoiner vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/supplements">Email apps for supplement stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs Sendlane FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
